   "body": "// Recognize\nCould you imagine that—\n\nCapable, calloused hands\nLimestone in your knuckles\nSore and content from a long days work \nLaying plumb lines in the fading sun\nThe only way you know to prepare\nBuilding for Mary, your bride-to-be\n\n// Remember\nCould you imagine that—\n\nConfident, calloused hands\nPacking your tools away,\nWalking—no skipping—to your dad's house,\nOnly to find your betrothed crying.\nTears on her face, but not of terror.\nJoyful tears. A tremendous wonder.\n\n“Overshadowed,” she whispers slowly,\n\"A Holy One to be born... a son...\"\nThe future you squared with line and cord\nCollapses to rubble at your feet\n\n// Remember\nCould you imagine that—\n\nShamed, calloused hands\nNot really grasping on\nAway from her, alone with the law, \n\"Divorce\" you read. This is the way. But...\nMake the parting quiet, merciful.\n\"A righteous man\"—you say—\"it must be.\"\n\nYour certain future slipping away,\nYour rough, calloused fists slam into stone,\nYour good name, your family honor,\nGone before you even speak a word.\n\n//Reframe\nCould you imagine that—\n\nChilled, calloused hands\nCovered in blood and tears,\nReady to resign, but a bright light.\nYour hands go up to shield in blindness.\n“Joseph, son of David\", The light says\n\"Do not be afraid to take embrace\".\n\n\"The One Conceived is from the Spirit\"\nYou pause. \"She will give birth to a Son\"\n\"You are to give him the name Jesus.\n\"He will save His people from their sins\"\n\n// Reframe and Rest\nCould you imagine that—\n\nComforted, calloused hands\nPalms sweaty, but open\nThe terror gone but a renewed heart\nYou play back what the angel declared\n\"And they will call Him Immanuel\"\n\"God with us\" you say \"Hallelujah\"\n\nYou wake up and your life is now clear\nYou take Mary home to be your wife\nNow waiting for the birth of the Son\nAnd you will give Him the name Jesus.\n\nCould you imagine that—"
